    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## RM \u00b7 9 \u2014 Instagram carousels\n\n**Two ways in:**\n- **webhook** `rm-publish-carousel` \u2014 post one now, given `caption` + `slide_urls`\n- **Daily 09:10** \u2014 asks the gateway whether an approved carousel is due today\n\n**Every slide URL must be publicly reachable.** Meta fetches each image at publish time, so localhost\nand private repos fail \u2014 slides are rendered locally and uploaded to Cloudflare R2.\n\n**Claim-then-confirm:** `/carousel/due` marks an item claimed *before* handing it over and only\n`/carousel/done` marks it published, so a crash between the two leaves it unserved rather than served\ntwice. Posting the same carousel twice cannot be undone.\n\nLimits: 2\u201310 slides, images and video may be mixed, and the whole carousel counts as **one** of the\n100 posts allowed per 24h.",
        "height": 390,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "overview-note",
      "name": "What this workflow does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Publish an Instagram carousel\n\nPOST to the webhook with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"caption\": \"\u2026\",\n  \"slide_urls\": [\"https://\u2026/01.jpg\", \"\u2026\"]\n}\n```\n\n**Every slide URL must be publicly reachable.** Meta cURLs each one at publish time \u2014 localhost and\nprivate repos fail. Rendered slides come from `social/carousel.py`; they have to be hosted somewhere\npublic first.\n\nLimits (Meta): 2\u201310 children, images and video may be mixed, and the whole carousel counts as ONE of\nthe 100 posts allowed per 24 hours.\n\nThe single-image publisher (`RM: Publish ready posts to Instagram`) is untouched \u2014 this is a sibling,\nnot a rewrite, so a carousel bug can never take the daily queue down with it.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "note",
      "name": "How this works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -640,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "rm-publish-carousel",
        "responseMode": "lastNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "hook",
      "name": "carousel",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -180,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "pythonNative",
        "pythonCode": "# One output item per slide, so the next HTTP node runs once per child container.\n# Validation lives here rather than in the HTTP node because a 400 from Meta half way through a\n# carousel leaves orphaned containers and no post.\n# the webhook wraps its payload in `body`; the scheduler branch hands it over flat\nbody = _items[0]['json'].get('body') or _items[0]['json']\nurls = body.get('slide_urls') or []\ncaption = body.get('caption') or ''\n\nif isinstance(urls, str):\n    urls = [u.strip() for u in urls.split(',') if u.strip()]\nif len(urls) < 2 or len(urls) > 10:\n    raise ValueError('a carousel needs between 2 and 10 slides, got %d' % len(urls))\nfor u in urls:\n    if not u.startswith('https://'):\n        raise ValueError('every slide must be a public https URL: %s' % u)\n\nreturn [{'json': {'url': u, 'index': i + 1, 'total': len(urls), 'caption': caption}}\n        for i, u in enumerate(urls)]"
      },
      "id": "split",
      "name": "One item per slide",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        40,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
